# ESP-IDF build output
firmware/build/
firmware/build-*/
firmware/sdkconfig
firmware/sdkconfig.old
firmware/managed_components/

# firmware/dependencies.lock is NOT ignored. It records the exact component
# versions a build resolved, and joltwallet/littlefs decides the on-disk
# filesystem format — an unpinned upgrade is a silently reformatted partition
# on the first boot after an OTA.

# Generated LVGL fonts. The sources of truth are tools/fonts/icons.txt and
# tools/fonts/generate.sh; the generated sources would otherwise add ~1.1 MB
# of unreviewable hex to every glyph-list change, permanently.
# Run tools/fonts/generate.sh before building the firmware.
firmware/components/slate_theme/assets/slate_font_*.c
firmware/components/slate_theme/assets/slate_icons.h

# Font generation scratch — upstream TTFs are fetched, not vendored
tools/fonts/.work/

# The editor's dependencies and its build output. The bundle is a ~200 KB
# single-file document generated from editor/src; the firmware build compresses
# whatever is in dist/ into the image (DESIGN.md §10), so it is generated
# before a build the way the fonts above are.
# Run tools/editor/build.sh before building the firmware.
editor/node_modules/
editor/dist/

# The flashing page's vendored ESP Web Tools bundle and the directory
# tools/flasher/build.sh assembles for deployment. dist/ contains a copy of the
# firmware images as well, so it is build output twice over: flasher/index.html
# and flasher/package-lock.json are the sources of truth, and
# .github/workflows/release.yml regenerates the rest on every tag.
flasher/node_modules/
flasher/dist/

.DS_Store

# Python bytecode from the helpers in tools/
__pycache__/

# Scratch notes agents pass between themselves while working the same
# repository — plans, todo lists, half-finished findings. They belong to a
# workspace rather than to a change, so `git add -A` must not sweep them into
# the repository's history. Unanchored on purpose: scratch is scratch wherever
# it sits, and nothing tracked is named .context.
.context/
